    },
    {
      "id": "08f1e3e8d87c6b0d39665a287499248e19c5dd63",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 712475215,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I have a capture file from Wireshark on macOS which someone provided me, which has certainly got such packets.\n\nI assumed (wrongly) that Linux would suffer the same issue but on closer inspection it doesn't, at least on my machine. Most of the larger packets don't have any data returned and I'm not seeing any over 256 KiB. However, I don't see anything in the usbmon documentation which suggests there is any hard limit on how much data it can return. Looking at the code, the de-facto limit is 1/5th the size of the usbmon ring buffer, which can be changed by ioctl within certain limits. I haven't tried changing it to see if I can capture bigger packets.\n\nI haven't tested on FreeBSD but assumed the problem may exist there too.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6273525,
            "username": "amachronic",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "amachronic",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3d16a3dc14dba1263c3ef723bb69fc19b7145fb75885eeda00e14520fcf77e1c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/amachronic"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-10-24T22:34:03.201Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-10-24T22:34:03.201Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 122707376,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4802,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0ed66603988bb9b01db656839a133eecad379d9a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 712475785,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Looking at the code, the de-facto limit is 1/5th the size of the usbmon ring buffer\n\nOh, yes, *that*.  I wondered what they were thinking when I saw that....\n\nNote that similar changes should be made to libpcap.",
          "author": {
